<h1>Usage of PageVariable Objects</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> There are two ways of using PageVariable object - as single and as multiple page report:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Single page report</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This is the case when no <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MainImage</i></span> object is included in the XML template. Report wizard consists only of one step  to select the XML template and optionally change the values of <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Variable</i></span> and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects. In this case all <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects will be printed on a single page. See the example below:</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="../images/single_page_table.gif" width="302px" height="93px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""><span style="font-style:italic;"><i><br>
PageVariable</i></span> objects</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example of single page report</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP221102555" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/single_page_report.gif" width="854px" height="598px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""><br>
Single page report</p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US">T</span>he report includes thumbnails of <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 1</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 2</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 3</b></span>, and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 4</b></span> in the only report page  used in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects.</p>
<p class="Code">XML Template Code:</p>
<p class="Code">&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?&gt;<br>
&lt;form&gt;<br>
&lt;Page unit="mm" size="9" orientation="landscape" offsetx="-5" offsety="-5"/&gt;<span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><br>
&lt;PageVariable x="31" y="18" width="125" height="75" name="TopLeft" contents="New page 1"/&gt;<br>
&lt;PageVariable x="160" y="18" width="125" height="75" name="TopRight" contents="New page 2"/&gt;<br>
&lt;PageVariable x="31" y="100" width="125" height="75" name="BottomLeft" contents="New page 3"/&gt;<br>
&lt;PageVariable x="160" y="100" width="125" height="75" name="BottomRight" contents="New page 4"/&gt;</font></span><br>
&lt;/form&gt;</p>
<p><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects are displayed in blue.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Multiple page report</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This is the case when one <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MainImage</i></span> object is included in the XML template. Report wizard consists of two steps  (1) to select the XML template and optionally change the values of <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Variable</i></span> and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects and (2) to add existing inspection pages to the report. In this case all <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects will be printed on every page together with the <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MainImage</i></span> for every selected page. See the examples below:</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="../images/multiple_page_table.gif" width="362px" height="233px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""><span style="font-style:italic;"><i><br>
PageVariable</i></span> (bounded in red) and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Variable</i></span> objects</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example of multiple page report</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP224914550" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/multiple_page_report1.gif" width="852px" height="604px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""><br>
Multiple page report (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>General</b></span> page)</p>
<p><img src="../images/multiple_page_report2.gif" width="852px" height="604px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""><br>
Multiple page report (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>S 0.0000</b></span> page)</p>
<p><img src="../images/multiple_page_report3.gif" width="852px" height="604px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""><br>
Multiple page report (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>S 50.0000</b></span> page)</p>
</div>
<p>The report includes <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>General</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>S 0.0000</b></span>, and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>S 50.0000</b></span> pages  used in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MainImage</i></span> object and thumbnails of <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 1</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>New page 2</b></span> in every report page  used in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects.</p>
